The army's movement, fighting and retreat run on lib.groups (ai/lib/groups.lua: forming, legs, per-unit targets,
the raid flight, the retreat), standing in for EECPAttackGroup / EECPAttackSubGroup / the ASG* state machines.

DEVIATION (fog) at the start: the C++ classic's forest finder and resource centres read the whole map; the port sees
what is explored (a town centre's few tiles at the start), so an idle citizen with nothing known to gather explores
(econ.lua) until the finders know a resource.

Interface additions for this port (docs/AI_LUA_UNITS.md §11): ai.tuning(), ai.techs{epoch, id}, ai.epoch(n),
ai.find_site's `margin` and `far` options, ai.class's `tech`, the own units' `target` and `gathers`, the view's
`income_total`, ai.gatherers() (the own gatherers per resource: ai.resource's `workers` counts the classic runners'
lists only, which never hold a script's units).

Interface gaps met (not added): the engine's combat state; the morale effect's fill; the continent manager's forests,
choke points and hills; the water site tiles; the gather goal's storage-search hook (BuildSettlementFor); the epoch's
SOL count (AddSOL); a resource's users at work (GetResourceUsers) as distinct from the gatherers sent.
